{"base_rate":0.39365918097754293,"brier":0.16786142668428003,"bss":0.29674355763185223,"bss_hi":0.39356243284235726,"bss_lo":0.18106665773220323,"country":"FI","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12540290620871863,"ess":455.1588185096054,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tampere</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tampere rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTAMPERE HARMALA, 4.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.30, ranked 62 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(38&ndash;92) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>229</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tampere</b> <span class=\"muted\">FI</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.30</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>38&ndash;92\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tampere &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tampere\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.78488687782806,378.70588235294116 86.36657894736842,329.3157894736842 145.84444444444443,256.17283950617286 263.6460526315789,128.15789473684214 354.9772972972973,47.51351351351349 409.4957205240175,18.0 409.4957205240175,24.358078602620083 354.9772972972973,106.54054054054052 263.6460526315789,209.57894736842107 145.84444444444443,323.58024691358025 86.36657894736842,372.42105263157896 58.78488687782806,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"238.70805812417439\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"238.70805812417439\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.78488687782806,365.52941176470586 86.36657894736842,338.89473684210526 145.84444444444443,274.14814814814815 263.6460526315789,219.1578947368421 354.9772972972973,155.72972972972974 409.4957205240175,103.8340611353712\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 221 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.78488687782806\" cy=\"365.52941176470586\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"86.36657894736842\" cy=\"338.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 30% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"145.84444444444443\" cy=\"274.14814814814815\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 58%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"263.6460526315789\" cy=\"219.1578947368421\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"354.9772972972973\" cy=\"155.72972972972974\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 229 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.4957205240175\" cy=\"103.8340611353712\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(39%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Tampere the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.40) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.13).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.126</td><td class='num'>16.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.233</td><td class='num'>10.9%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.395</td><td class='num'>9.6%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.405</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":61.49911,"lon":23.78712,"n":757,"n_cities":109,"name":"Tampere","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0022171945701357464,"n":221,"obs":0.04524886877828054,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08013157894736843,"n":76,"obs":0.11842105263157894,"sig":false},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.24814814814814817,"n":81,"obs":0.2962962962962963,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7260000000000008,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5809210526315789,"n":76,"obs":0.4473684210526316,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.7260000000000008,"mean":0.8389189189189189,"n":74,"obs":0.6216216216216216,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9929